# Conditional SHACL data quality rules (IF guard)

Context: Data Quality rules applied to every instance of their target entity.
There was no way to say "this constraint only applies when another attribute
holds a given value" — the only `sh:condition` in the codebase sat on SHACL-AF
inference rules, not on validation. Conformance and consistency rules can now
carry an optional list of conditions, built the way decision-table conditions
are built in Business Rules. Design: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-03-conditional-shacl-rules-design.md`.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/ShapeConditions.py`
   New module owning the guard: shape-dict accessors, validation, the SQL
   subject filter, the in-memory subject filter, and the `sh:SPARQLTarget`
   query. Reuses the decision-table operator maps (`DT_OP_SQL`,
   `DT_STRING_OPS`, `DT_NUMERIC_OPS`) plus `exists` / `notExists`, so the two
   rule builders share one operator vocabulary instead of inventing a third.
2. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/SHACLService.py`
   `shape_to_sql()` extracted into `_base_shape_sql()` and now wraps the
   constraint query in `SELECT v.* FROM (...) v WHERE v.s IN (<guard>)`.
   Attribute conditions use `LEFT JOIN` so `or` logic cannot drop subjects
   missing one property; `exists` / `notExists` compile to `EXISTS` subqueries.
3. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/SHACLService.py`
   `evaluate_shape_in_memory()` extracted into `_base_shape_violations()` and
   now filters its violations down to the guarded subjects. `create_shape()`
   persists `conditions` / `condition_logic`; `import_shapes_with_report()`
   added.
4. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/SHACLGenerator.py`
   `_add_conditional_shape()` emits a guarded shape as its own node shape with
   a `sh:target [ a sh:SPARQLTarget ]`, since its focus nodes are a subset of
   the class. Unconditional shapes are still grouped one node shape per class.
   The query uses full IRIs — prefixes inside a `sh:select` resolve from
   `sh:prefixes`, not from the enclosing document.
5. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/SHACLParser.py`
   `parse_with_report()` counts shapes arriving with a SPARQL target and
   recovers their target class from the query, so an imported conditional rule
   keeps a usable constraint instead of landing without a target. Conditions
   themselves are not reconstructed.
6. `src/back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py`
   `validate_shape()` rejects conditions on unsupported dimensions, on a shape
   with no target entity, with an unknown operator, with no property, or with
   an empty value on a comparison operator.
7. `src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py`
   The save route forwards `conditions` / `condition_logic`; the import route
   reports how many shapes lost their conditions and now apply to every
   instance.
8. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-conditions.js`
   New `ConditionRowsModule`: reusable property/operator/value rows with
   `render` / `collect` / `addRow` / `summarize`. Rows live in the DOM, wired by
   delegation. Selecting a relationship narrows the operators to
   `exists` / `notExists` and hides the value input.
9. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-dataquality.js`
   IF block rendered for conformance and consistency only; conditions collected
   on save, restored on edit, summarised on the rule card and in the
   auto-generated message, and previewed as the `sh:SPARQLTarget` the backend
   will emit. `_localName()` / `_isObjectProperty()` extracted so the condition
   property list and `_populatePropertySelect()` share one implementation.
10. `src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_dataquality.html`
    `#dqConditionBlock` with an All/Any logic toggle, a rows container and an
    "Add condition" button, between the property select and the constraint
    fields.
11. `src/front/templates/ontology.html`
    Loads `ontology-conditions.js` before `ontology-dataquality.js`.
12. `tests/units/ontology/test_dataquality.py`
    Conditional SQL (wrapping, numeric cast, `NOT EXISTS`, `or` + `LEFT JOIN`,
    unconditional regression), in-memory filtering (and/or, exists/notExists,
    incomplete rows ignored), and the `validate_shape` rejection cases.
13. `tests/back/core/w3c/shacl/test_shacl_generator.py`
    SPARQL target emission, constraint preserved, no `sh:targetClass` on a
    guarded shape, plain shapes still grouped, and the import drop report.
14. `tests/units/front/test_dq_condition_builder.py`
    Source contracts for the shared builder: exposed API, operator vocabulary,
    hidden value input, relationship operator narrowing, DOM-aligned collect,
    dimension restriction, and script load order.

