## Honour the selected dimensions for SWRL, decision table and aggregate rules

Context: Running the data quality checks with only **Conformance** ticked still
executed every SWRL rule, whose results are filed under Structural. SHACL
shapes have a checkbox each and were filtered correctly, but SWRL rules,
decision tables and aggregate rules have no checkbox of their own — the route
collected all of them unconditionally. The frontend made it worse: as soon as a
domain had any shape it sent `shape_ids` *instead of* `dimensions`, so the
backend had no selection left to apply to those three families.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/constants.py`
   Add `SWRL_CATEGORY` and `BUSINESS_RULE_CATEGORY`, naming the dimension each
   non-SHACL rule family reports under, instead of leaving it implicit in the
   result dicts the runner builds.
2. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   `start_dataquality_checks()` gates the three families on the selected
   dimensions: SWRL rules need `structural`, decision tables and aggregate
   rules need `conformance`. A request naming no dimension still runs
   everything, so external API callers are unaffected.
3. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   A selection matching nothing now reports "Nothing to check in the selected
   dimensions." rather than claiming the domain has no rules at all.
4. `src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js`
   `runAllChecks()` always sends `dimensions`, adding `shape_ids` when
   individual rules are picked, and only refuses to run when both are empty —
   a dimension holding just SWRL rules can now run on its own.
5. `tests/units/api/test_dq_run_selection.py`
   New module driving the route with a stubbed domain and task manager:
   Conformance excludes the SWRL rules but keeps the business rules, Structural
   does the reverse, named rules still honour the dimensions, and no selection
   runs everything. Reverting the gate fails 5 of them.
6. `tests/units/front/test_dq_run_payload.py`
   New node-executed module asserting the request carries the dimensions
   alongside the rule ids.

