================================================================================
Data quality runs on one execution target
================================================================================

Context:
The Data Quality page let the user pick between a "Triple-Store" and a "Graph"
backend. That stopped being an engine choice once the product grew several
graph engines: the two buttons opened different stores over *different data*.
"Triple-Store" ran SQL on the Delta VIEW (the triples mapped from the source
tables), while "Graph" loaded the domain's graph — base plus anything reasoning
had inferred — into the app process and evaluated the shapes in Python. The
same rule could therefore return different counts depending on the button, and
nothing in the UI said so.

The two paths were not equivalent either. The in-memory one could not evaluate
`sh:datatype` or `sh:sparql` at all, and it was the default. On a Neo4j domain
it also could not run SWRL rules, decision tables or aggregate rules, because
those are still pushed as SQL through `execute_query`, which Neo4j refuses.
And it held every triple in RAM for the duration of the run.

The triple-store VIEW is created by every build whatever graph engine the
domain uses, so it is the one target every domain has. Checks now always
compile to SQL and run against it.

Changes:
1. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
   `run_data_quality_task()` drops its `requested_backend` parameter and always
   opens the `view` store to run `run_sql_checks`.
2. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
   Removed `run_graph_checks()` and the three rule-family helpers it drove
   (`_run_swrl_graph_checks`, `_run_dt_graph_checks`, `_run_agg_graph_checks`),
   plus `_count_class_population_graph` — 537 lines that existed only to serve
   the removed branch.
3. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   New `_dataquality_table()` resolves the VIEW server-side and rejects an
   unbuilt domain with "Build the Knowledge Graph first." Both
   `start_dataquality_checks` and `execute_dataquality_check` use it and no
   longer read `backend` or a client-supplied `triplestore_table`.
4. `src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py`
   The public `DataQualityRequest.backend` field is marked deprecated and
   ignored rather than removed, so existing API clients keep working.
5. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/__init__.py`, `src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLEngine.py`
   Dropped the `run_graph_checks` re-export and the docstring pointing at it.
6. `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_dataquality.html`
   The backend button group is replaced by the resolved table name and a hint
   that reasoning output is out of scope.
7. `src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js`
   Removed `_initBackendToggle` and `_getSelectedBackend`; the request no
   longer names a backend or a table.
8. `tests/units/api/test_dq_run_selection.py`
   New `TestExecutionTarget`: the VIEW is the target, a client-supplied table
   or backend is ignored, and an unbuilt domain is rejected.
9. `tests/units/front/test_dq_run_payload.py`
   New `TestExecutionTarget`: the request carries neither `backend` nor
   `triplestore_table`, and a domain with a graph but no VIEW cannot run.
10. `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/features.md`, `docs/INFO.md`
   Describe the single execution path. Also corrected the claim that the
   product validates via PySHACL — it has no production caller; execution has
   always been the hand-rolled SQL translator.

