================================================================================
Rule SQL: TRY_CAST so one non-numeric value cannot fail a whole rule
================================================================================

Context:

Running the "Monthly fee between 1 and 10" rule on the deployed app reported
"Query execution failed for this decision table", with no way to see why.

Every object in the triple store is a string, so any numeric comparison has to
cast. All the rule SQL builders emitted a bare ``CAST(... AS DOUBLE)``.
Databricks warehouses run with ANSI mode on, where a bare CAST aborts the whole
statement on the first value it cannot convert — so a single ``"free"`` in a fee
column takes down the entire rule instead of simply not matching it. This became
reachable for every engine once data quality standardised on SQL against the
VIEW earlier today (previously some of this ran in memory or on Lakebase).

The generic failure message compounded it: the cause was only in the server log,
so a broken rule and a warehouse problem looked identical in the UI.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py`
   New ``sql_numeric(expr, sql_type="DOUBLE")`` emitting ``TRY_CAST``, with the
   ANSI-mode rationale stated once. Exported from `back.core.helpers`.
2. `src/back/core/reasoning/DecisionTableEngine.py`
   Numeric condition cells use ``sql_numeric`` — this is the reported failure.
3. `src/back/core/reasoning/AggregateRuleEngine.py`
   All five aggregate/HAVING casts are now ``TRY_CAST``.
4. `src/back/core/reasoning/SPARQLRuleEngine.py`
   Numeric FILTER comparisons use ``sql_numeric``.
5. `src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLBuiltinRegistry.py`
   16 SQL templates switched to ``TRY_CAST`` (comparison, math, date built-ins).
   Cypher templates untouched.
6. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/ShapeConditions.py`
   Conditional IF-block numeric guards use ``sql_numeric``; they shipped this
   morning with the same defect.
7. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
   New ``_sql_error_detail`` / ``_failed_check_result``: a failed check now
   reports the engine's message (one line, capped at 300 chars) and keeps its
   SQL so the UI's code button works. Replaces the four near-identical
   "Query execution failed for this X." blocks (shape, SWRL, DT, aggregate).
8. `src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js`
   Message cell carries the full text as a tooltip.
9. `src/front/static/query/css/query-reasoning.css`
   ``.dq-col-msg`` clamps to two lines so a long engine error stays scannable.

Tests:

10. `tests/units/ontology/test_business_rules.py`
    Decision-table numeric cells and aggregate SUM emit ``TRY_CAST`` and no bare
    ``CAST``.
11. `tests/units/ontology/test_swrl_engine.py`
    New ``TestBuiltinNumericCasts``: no registered built-in emits a bare CAST.
12. `tests/units/ontology/test_shape_conditions.py`
    Numeric condition assertion tightened to ``TRY_CAST``.
13. `tests/units/ontology/test_dataquality.py`
    New ``TestFailedCheckReporting``: engine message reaches the row, SQL is
    kept, multi-line errors collapse, long errors truncate, silent exceptions
    still name themselves.

