## Use TRY_CAST for DQ numeric SQL and surface engine errors

Context: ANSI-mode warehouses abort a whole data-quality statement on the
first non-numeric triple value when rules use bare CAST. Failed checks also
only reported a generic message, so users needed the server log to diagnose.
Numeric rule SQL now uses TRY_CAST, and failed checks carry the engine error
(and SQL) in the result row.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py`
   Added `sql_numeric()` helper wrapping `TRY_CAST(... AS DOUBLE)`.
2. `src/back/core/helpers/__init__.py`
   Re-export `sql_numeric`.
3. `src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLBuiltinRegistry.py`
   SWRL builtin SQL templates use TRY_CAST for numeric/date casts.
4. `src/back/core/reasoning/DecisionTableEngine.py`
   Numeric decision-table conditions use `sql_numeric()`.
5. `src/back/core/reasoning/SPARQLRuleEngine.py`
   Numeric FILTER comparisons use `sql_numeric()`.
6. `src/back/core/reasoning/AggregateRuleEngine.py`
   Aggregate numeric casts use TRY_CAST.
7. `src/back/core/w3c/shacl/ShapeConditions.py`
   Conditional SHACL numeric guards use `sql_numeric()`.
8. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
   `_failed_check_result` / `_sql_error_detail` surface the engine message on
   failed DQ checks (SHACL, SWRL, DT, aggregate).
9. `src/front/static/query/css/query-reasoning.css`
   Clamp long DQ result messages to two lines (full text on tooltip).
10. `src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js`
    Minor alignment with failed-check message display.
11. `tests/units/ontology/test_business_rules.py`
    Assert TRY_CAST in DT/aggregate SQL.
12. `tests/units/ontology/test_swrl_engine.py`
    Assert no bare CAST in SWRL builtin SQL templates.
13. `tests/units/ontology/test_shape_conditions.py`
    Expect TRY_CAST for numeric condition SQL.
14. `tests/units/ontology/test_dataquality.py`
    Cover failed-check reporting helpers.

